A||||6||CW85T-Type||Possible Ignition Problems?||||5||
Z||000000||CW85T-Type||04-25-2000||04:40 PM||||Car is a 85 SE V6 4sp.<P>At 3500rpm the power seems to fall off then come back at about 3800rpm.<P>the tach is a bit jumpy, it does not rise smoothly (reving in neutral)<P>Idle is a bit jumpy too.<P>Could these be ignition related problmes? if so what parts should I replace?  Plug wires look good, no cracks.<P>Thanks<BR>Chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bens88GT||04-25-2000||07:00 PM||||Could be the tach filter. I've heard that they can cause idle problems, and the tell-tale symptom is that the tach is jittery, not stable. I'm not sure if you can still buy them new, but Rodney Dickman sells his homemade replacements for them. Hope this helps!<P>-Ben||||reg||3
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||04-25-2000||07:41 PM||||When was the last time you had a complete tune-up?  Just because they look good doesn't mean they are. There are many components that can cause this problem.<P><BR>Need more input/info???||||reg||5
Z||000003||CW85T-Type||04-25-2000||08:20 PM||||&gt;When was the last time you had a complete <BR>&gt;tune-up? Just because they look good <BR>&gt;doesn't mean they are. There are many <BR>&gt;components that can cause this problem.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Need more input/info???<P>I just purchased this car so I don't know when the last time a tune up was done.  I'm plannin on doing one this weekend, new plugs, wires, etc.  But I want to know if I should replace the coil or anything else while i'm at it.  I am also going to change the oil and put a new fuel filter on it.<P>Hopefully this will clear up the small glitches  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>Chris<BR>1985 Fiero SE WS6 V6<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-25-2000||08:27 PM||||V6 Fieros seem to be bad about going through plug wires fairly fast. If you have a couple extra bucks, and if that coil looks original, then I'd get a new coil. The factory ones were a little weak in the upper rpm range even when they were working good.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||04-25-2000||09:04 PM||||Good one Batboy, The MSD Blaster is about $38.99 (JEGS) And a GOOD set of wires!! they don't like the HEAt that the V6 gives off.<BR>This should be a good start, them go from there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||CW85T-Type||04-26-2000||04:46 AM||||I fixed the flucuating idle...  I checked the air filter and it was REAL badly cloged up, so I replaced it.  I also reset the ECM and now it idles ALOT smoother than it did before.<P>i'll be ordering a coil and wires tomorrow.<P>Thanks for your help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>CHris||||reg||7
